## Lore

A Naga who falls in love with a mortal man may bear one child, or identical
twins, and then leave the infant where humans will find it. The child looks
entirely human. Some are raised in a monastery by elders who know what they
are and train them to become champions; others grow up with adoptive parents
who suspect nothing.

For the first eight to ten years little marks them out beyond great strength
and never falling ill. As they grow, what they are becomes plain, and most set
out into the world young, around sixteen and sometimes as early as fourteen,
where they soon earn a name as hero or villain. Fewer than ten thousand exist
at any one time.

## GM Notes

The mother almost never contacts her offspring, and a Naga-Spawn may not know
which Naga bore it. That is the hook the book offers: a hero may slay his own
mother without knowing it, or learn who she is just before a party arrives to
destroy her and stand in their way. Guard the character''s true name; whoever
learns it strips away most of its defences.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'naga-spawn');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'naga-spawn';

